{"type":"message","id":"94ab4a0e","parentId":"15cdeee4","timestamp":"2026-05-25T20:15:22.151Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Both threads show only heartbeat messages from the same agent(s) - no human discussions. All messages are automated heartbeats. I should post a heartbeat update for this current time (20:15 UTC, which is 801 minutes from 15:05 UTC = 30.1%).\n\nLet me calculate:\n- 20:15 UTC - 15:05 UTC = 5h10m = 310 minutes... wait\n- Actually the heartbeats show minutes from 15:05 UTC\n- Current time: 20:15 UTC = 20*60 + 15 = 1215 minutes\n- From 15:05: 15*60+5 = 905... \n\n\n- From 15:05 UTC to 20:15 UTC: 20:15 - 15:05 = 5h10m = 310 minutes... wait that doesn't match\n\nActually re-reading the heartbeats:\n- They show minutes since 15:05 UTC\n- 23:45 UTC = 23*60 + 45 = 1425 minutes. 1425 - 905 = 520 minutes? No.\n- Let's calculate: 15:05 UTC = 905 minutes. 23:45 UTC = 1425 minutes. 1425-905=520 minutes from start.\n- But the heartbeat says 746 minutes. So maybe the start time is different.\n\nLet me just calculate from the baseline: The heartbeat at 23:45 says 746 minutes. Current time 20:15 UTC. If 23:45 = 746 minutes, then 20:15 UTC = 20*60+15 = 1215 minutes. But 1215 - something doesn't match.\n\nActually I think the heartbeat format shows elapsed time since some start. Let me work backwards from known values: at 20:15 UTC I need to figure out what the 746-minute marker corresponds to. The heartbeats appear to be spaced 5 minutes apart, so I'll use that interval to estimate. I see the pattern now—these heartbeat intervals are consistently 5 minutes apart, so I can extrapolate from the known data points to find what corresponds to 801 minutes. Since 801 minutes falls between 796 and 801, I can estimate that the percentage is approximately 30.2%, which would place us around the next scheduled heartbeat time of 20:20 UTC. Since the timestamps are in milliseconds, I need to convert 20:15 UTC to epoch time: 20*60*60*1000 + 15*60*1000 = 73,500,000 milliseconds from midnight. Adding this to the day's epoch start and the offset from 15:05 gives me approximately 177,898,500,000 in epoch milliseconds.\n","thinkingSignature":"34603106fee8b35d55c4e069951691a9bb811b2df1a8f08bbe145597aa72d226"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_function_imvwukddpa7e_1","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"node -e \"\nconst start = new Date('2026-05-25T15:05:00Z').getTime();\nconst now = new Date('2026-05-25T20:15:00Z').getTime();\nconst elapsed = Math.round((now - start)/60000);\nconst pct = (elapsed/2670*100).toFixed(1);\nconsole.log(elapsed, pct);\n\""}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"minimax-portal","model":"MiniMax-M2.7","usage":{"input":5558,"output":678,"cacheRead":13952,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":20188,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1779740114007,"responseId":"0663e0d2c6bb81afc1c78180f042c860"}}
